generics: Generic functions

A generic function becomes a C++ function for each list of type arguments that the program
names, an instance: gp_inst_<hash>_Map, with the hash taken from the package, the file and
the type arguments. The instance is lowered as if the function were written with those
types, so a + b, T(x), len(s), x.M() and any(x) mean what they mean for those Go types.
Types are not C++ template parameters, because int and int64 are one C++ type (int64_t)
while Go tells them apart (type switches, %T, interfaces).

Each use of the function asks for its instance by name; the instance is written once in the
unit of the file that first needed it, and a comment names it in Go's notation (//
Map[int,string]). The annotation on the generic function's line lists every instance made
from that body, and each call site says which instance it calls.

A type argument that is a C/C++ type makes a C++ function template that the C++ compiler
deduces instead (Phase 07 README, C/C++ type arguments).

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#generics-steps-71-and-72
See also: gocpp explain interfaces, gocpp explain interop
Also known as: generic, instance, instances, typeparams

Example (generics.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    func Map[T, U any](xs []T, f func(T) U) []U {
    	out := make([]U, 0, len(xs))
    	for _, x := range xs {
    		out = append(out, f(x))
    	}
    	return out
    }

    type Big [64]int

    // Show has one C++ function for each type argument: with Big (512 bytes) the captured y is boxed,
    // with int and string it is copied into the lambda.
    func Show[T any](x T) {
    	var y T = x
    	f := func() T { return y }
    	fmt.Println(any(f()))
    }

    func main() {
    	Show(1)
    	Show(Big{})
    	Show("s")
    	fmt.Println(Map([]int{1, 2, 3}, func(i int) string { return fmt.Sprint(i * 2) }))
    	fmt.Println(Map([]string{"a"}, func(s string) int { return len(s) }))
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    struct Big;

    struct Big : gp::newtype<Big, gp::array<int64_t, 64>> {
        using gp::newtype<Big, gp::array<int64_t, 64>>::newtype;
    };
    static_assert(sizeof(Big) == 512 && alignof(Big) == 8);

    extern const gp::type_desc gp_td_Big;
    extern const gp::type_desc* const gp_tdc_0;
    extern const gp::type_desc* const gp_tdc_1;
    void main();

    } // namespace gpkg_main
